{"id":28065,"slug":"ministry-of-fear","title":"Ministry of Fear","year":1944,"country":"United States","duration":87,"spine":649,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/28065-ministry-of-fear","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/1a5c01f75aef9b18d08f9ccbf5561972/zVKSQvVRaxcsqWeU0EVzXYRkFFxWSp_large.jpg","description":"Suffused with dread and paranoia, this Fritz Lang adaptation of a novel by Graham Greene is a plunge into the eerie shadows of a world turned upside down by war. En route to London after being released from a mental institution, Stephen Neale (Ray Milland) stops at a seemingly innocent village fair, after which he finds himself caught in the web of a sinister underworld with possible Nazi connections. Lang was among the most illustrious of the European émigré filmmakers working in Hollywood during World War II, and Ministry of Fear is one of his finest American productions, an unpredictable thriller with style to spare.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Fritz Lang","slug":"fritz-lang"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Ray Milland","role":"Stephen Neale","slug":"ray-milland"},{"actor":"Marjorie Reynolds","role":"Carla Hilfe","slug":"marjorie-reynolds"},{"actor":"Carl Esmond","role":"Willi Hilfe","slug":"carl-esmond"},{"actor":"Hillary Brooke","role":"Mrs. Bellane No. 2","slug":"hillary-brooke"},{"actor":"Percy Waram","role":"Inspector Prentice","slug":"percy-waram"},{"actor":"Dan Duryea","role":"Cost/Travers, the Tailor","slug":"dan-duryea"},{"actor":"Alan Napier","role":"Dr. J. M. Forrester","slug":"alan-napier"},{"actor":"Erskine Sanford","role":"George Rennit","slug":"erskine-sanford"},{"actor":"Aminta Dyne","role":"Mrs. Bellane No. 1","slug":"aminta-dyne"},{"actor":"Mary Field","role":"Martha Penteel","slug":"mary-field"}],"credits":[{"role":"Director","person":"Fritz Lang","slug":"fritz-lang"},{"role":"Associate producer","person":"Seton I. Miller","slug":null},{"role":"Screenplay","person":"Seton I. Miller","slug":null},{"role